  "narrative": "The new conditional estimates split the two remaining candidate lines. For feature_045/outcome_006, the approximate 10% clinical scale is about 0.0093 because the absolute mean of outcome_006 is about 0.093. H76/R68 is the strongest new result: within feature_042=1 and feature_027=0, the signed stronger-dependency estimate is +0.1063, with a 95% signed interval +0.0318 to +0.1809. The entire interval is above the clinical threshold and the point estimate is more than ten times the threshold. This is strong discovery evidence that feature_045=1 is associated with a much more negative outcome_006 score in this defined subgroup, but it is still a post-discovery conditional subgroup and the broader feature_027=0 feature_045 line (H67) failed independent validation. Therefore I accept H76 as a supplied-dataset association and request independent validation to determine whether this refined subgroup is stable or a context-specific artifact. I do not yet treat it as causal or generalizable.\n\nThe rest of the feature_045/outcome_006 conditional evidence is heterogeneous. H72/R66, within feature_027=1, has a signed negative estimate of about -0.0319 with interval -0.1169 to +0.0530. There is no clinically positive stronger-dependency association in feature_027=1, and this makes the feature_042=1 marginal signal (H69) much less attractive as a broad claim. H80/R69, within feature_042=1 and feature_027=1, is negative but extremely imprecise (n=22/53), so I keep it unresolved and deferred rather than interpreting the negative point strongly. H75/R67, the feature_042 interaction for feature_045/outcome_006, is positive in point size (+0.0619) but has interval -0.0205 to +0.1443 and therefore cannot establish effect modification. H81/R70 and H82/R71, within feature_042=1 split by feature_054 levels, have large positive points but intervals that include zero or below-threshold values; H82 is especially imprecise. These results suggest the H69/H76 signal is concentrated in the feature_042=1/feature_027=0 region and is not independently supported across feature_027=1. I therefore defer H69 and the other feature_045/outcome_006 interaction/stratum claims while awaiting independent validation of H76. If H76 fails validation, the feature_045/outcome_006 line should be closed as likely overfit/context-specific. If it passes, H76 becomes a narrow but defensible supplied-dataset association, and the broader H69 marginal remains only a context-dependent summary.\n\nFor feature_042/outcome_008, the approximate 10% clinical scale is about 0.0282. The accepted H60 signal (feature_042=1 associated with a weaker-dependency outcome_008 within feature_027=1) is supported by the new conditional splits. H79/R74 within feature_027=1 and feature_045=0 is +0.0722 (+0.0084 to +0.1360), and H78/R73 within feature_027=1 and feature_045=1 is +0.1027 (+0.0065 to +0.1989). Both are statistically positive and clinically large in point size, but their lower confidence bounds are below the approximate clinical threshold, and the feature_045=1 exposed cell is very small (n=22), so I keep them unresolved but active. H84/R75 and H85/R76 within feature_027=1 split by feature_054 levels are also positive and statistically positive (+0.0655, +0.0035 to +0.1275; +0.1172, +0.0153 to +0.2191), again with lower bounds below threshold. Together these direct strata make H60 look internally stable across measured feature_045 and feature_054 structure, which is important for the accepted subgroup claim. However, the feature_045 modification interaction H77/R72 is too wide to interpret (+0.0305, -0.0842 to +0.1452), so I cannot conclude that feature_045 modifies the feature_042 effect within feature_027=1. H87/R77, within feature_027=0 and feature_045=1, is positive but not statistically positive (+0.0392, -0.0089 to +0.0874), arguing against treating feature_042 as a broad outcome_008 marker outside the feature_027=1 context. I therefore keep H60 accepted and active, defer the overall heterogeneous feature_042 line, and prioritize validation of the strongest new discovery (H76) because it resolves whether the remaining feature_045/outcome_006 signal is real or an overfit conditional artifact. If validation remains useful later, H60 or a refined feature_027=1 subgroup would be the next candidate, but this iteration uses the single request on H76.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 6 appraise. Validation requested for H76: feature_045/outcome_006 stronger-dependency within feature_042=1 and feature_027=0. Discovery R68 +0.1063 CI +0.0318 to +0.1809, n=101/287; outcome_006 clinical threshold ~0.0093, whole interval above threshold. Accept H76 in supplied dataset, active pending validation. If H76 fails validation, close feature_045/outcome_006 line and reject H76; if passes, H76 is strong but narrow context-specific association.\n\nFeature_045/outcome_006 status: H69 marginal feature_042=1 unresolved deferred after H76 concentration and feature_027=1 negative/unstable. H72 feature_027=1 reject/closed: R66 -0.0319 CI -0.1169 to +0.0530, no clinically positive support. H80 tiny feature_042=1/feature_027=1 unresolved deferred: R69 -0.0575 CI -0.2700 to +0.1550, too imprecise. H75 feature_042 interaction unresolved deferred: R67 +0.0619 CI -0.0205 to +0.1443. H81 unresolved deferred: +0.0807 CI -0.0052 to +0.1666. H82 unresolved deferred: +0.0735 CI -0.0588 to +0.2059. H67 and H27 remain rejected/closed due failed validation and weak overall evidence.\n\nFeature_042/outcome_008: H60 accepted active. New conditional support: H79 feature_027=1/feature_045=0 unresolved active +0.0722 CI +0.0084 to +0.1360 (lower below threshold ~0.0282); H78 feature_027=1/feature_045=1 unresolved active +0.1027 CI +0.0065 to +0.1989, tiny exposed n=22; H84 feature_027=1/feature_054=level_001 unresolved active +0.0655 CI +0.0035 to +0.1275; H85 feature_027=1/feature_054=level_002 unresolved active +0.1172 CI +0.0153 to +0.2191. These support stability of H60 across feature_045 and feature_054, but lower bounds below clinical threshold keep them unresolved. H77 interaction within feature_027=1 by feature_045 unresolved deferred: +0.0305 CI -0.0842 to +0.1452, too imprecise. H87 feature_027=0/feature_045=1 unresolved deferred: +0.0392 CI -0.0089 to +0.0874, outside feature_027=1 weak. This argues feature_042 is not broad, but may be a genuine subgroup signal in feature_027=1.\n\nCurrent accepted robust: H30 feature_027=1 -> weaker-dependency outcome_014, validated; accepted strata H39/H40/H44/H45. H60 feature_042=1 -> weaker-dependency outcome_008 within feature_027=1 accepted, active. H76 newly accepted active pending validation.\n\nValidation budget: 5 before this request, 4 remaining after H76. Next validation priority if budget and plan permit: H60 or refined feature_027=1 subgroup if H76 result consumes interest or if feature_045 line closes. Broad feature_042/outcome_008 and feature_045/outcome_006 lines remain closed unless refined validation passes. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
